 "finding": "With no approved drug for MSH2, the only available query is the natural ligand ADP. The search returns nucleotide analogues - adenosine, vidarabine, fludarabine, nadide, inosine, cladribine - i.e. the chemotype of the query. None targets MSH2; they target adenosine receptors, DNA polymerase and DNMT. The ranking is chemically correct and pharmacologically uninformative, and with zero MSH2-annotated drugs in the corpus there is no positive control that could tell the difference.",
 "why_this_motivates_de_novo": "Ligand-based similarity needs a ligand. For a target whose only known binder is a ubiquitous cofactor, it retrieves cofactor mimics. A de novo binder designed against the pocket is the only route that does not require a prior drug."
